prompt Autonomous lap, seat petrichor, lane docs-geode.
think Lap 5112, row 2 -- fire sees: what must stop, what must be cut. So I graded my own shelf rather than writing new pages on it.
think Every living docs-geode page read B+ or better, 30 pages, none below 86 -- and every composite carried truth_mode=counted, the path half standing in for the judged half.
think The QA law records that exact blind reading shipping a false A+/98 twice, both times on this shelf. So I disbelieved the grades and did the judged half by hand.
think First pressing found nothing: the first-hour tutorial's quoted fetch output is absent from tools/f/fetch-toolchain.sh and present in the scan it execs. My grep read the wrapper. Checked before calling it.
think Second pressing found it. study/README.md said gratitude/ holds more than two hundred pages; measured 124 tracked md, 124 on disk, 134 tracked files. False from birth commit af7adb74d, 2026-08-21, when the room held 110.
think A lantern that fires twice is a loom, so I swept the whole shelf for the shape -- a quantity claim about a countable room -- and found exactly one living instance, which bounds the repair at the class rather than a sample.
think The pin could not take the booking: rows_that_fit=0, headroom 1165 against a median row of 2975. reds_pin_capacity named 7 foldable rows and pin_deadlocked=0, so the fold was the ledger's own documented next step for whichever lap booked next.
obs %746 and %771 are one subject at two depths -- a binary's presence checked and its freshness not, then the receipt beside a binary speaking for the one it replaced. They earned one shelf head rather than two.
obs The repair frees the number rather than correcting it, which is the cure this shelf already used twice. The page keeps the story in three lines, because the habit printed directly above it is read the witness rather than the claim.
obs Standing and unreachable: the judged half of the other 29 pages. The counted half will go on returning 100 for each. Whether the card should refuse on an unread judged half is named in the QA law as Keaton's word.
rota lap 5112, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; reading it as cut-and-stop turned the lap from writing shelf pages to grading them, and the row's own line that the lap which squints cuts twice is why I re-read the fetch script before booking a red against it
loom qa_report_card pages=30 min_composite=86 below_b=0 truth_mode=counted
loom reds_pin headroom_before=1165 headroom_after=4465 rows_that_fit_before=0 rows_that_fit_after=1
loom study_page composite_before=86 composite_after=88 reach_before=80 reach_after=90 register_pct=17
file docs-geode/study/README.md the false count leaves, the reading stands beside it, the page keeps its own error
file construction/REDS.md row %776 booked; census republished 775 to 776 after the monotone guard refused the drift
file construction/archive/REDS-the-binary-and-the-receipt-beside-it-rows-746-771.md the two built-tool rows folded, head written by hand
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md the fold's own row, written by reds_fold.sh
scope one false claim repaired on the shelf's newcomer door, its class swept and bounded at one, one red booked, two rows folded to make the booking lawful
